  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>EMIT is the IT organization of a major energy company. Its internal site, Inside EMIT, was how leadership communicated with thousands of IT employees — and it needed to be rebuilt. A predecessor site had set a new benchmark for storytelling and content inside the organization, but had a short lifespan. The rebuild had to carry that content forward and give the organization a durable platform for its three strategic pillars: culture, strategy, and learning &amp; growth.</p>

  <h2>The approach</h2>
  <p>The project ran in four phases over one quarter: initiation, discovery, planning and strategy, then design and development of Release 1.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Discovery</b> — reviewed existing research and analytics, then interviewed stakeholders, users, and the people who managed and contributed content. Findings were synthesized into proto-personas and read out to stakeholders.</li>
    <li><b>Planning &amp; strategy</b> — a joint work session with stakeholders: card sorting the existing content and experience mapping. Out of it came the content strategy and the finalized information architecture.</li>
    <li><b>Release 1</b> — wireframes, copy for the main pages, A/B homepage concepts, ten page templates, and development in two batches — live before the end of the year.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What success meant</h2>
  <p>Success was defined per pillar before any design started. For culture: leaders building trust through transparency, and employees feeling valued and able to decide without micromanagement. For strategy: every employee understanding where the organization is going and how their work fits. For learning &amp; growth: self-learning as a habit, and one place where every learning opportunity across the organization can be found.</p>

  <h2>The design</h2>
  <p>The site shipped as a news platform: a homepage feed of stories tagged by pillar, an About section explaining the organization and its strategic framework, leadership pages that put faces and voices to the names, and a filterable stories &amp; videos library.</p>

